 If you are interested in this opportunity, please forward your CV to resume@all\-european\-careers.com.










 Following countries are part of the European Union: Austria, Belgium, Bulgaria, Croatia, Republic of Cyprus, Czech Republic, Denmark, Estonia, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Hungary, Ireland, Italy, Latvia, Lithuania, Luxembourg, Malta, Netherlands, Poland, Portugal, Romania, Slovakia, Slovenia, Spain and Sweden.

**What We Do**
 Merantix Momentum is a Berlin\-based AI startup focusing on accelerating AI adoption across many industries through B2B solutions, as well as publicly funded research projects. We work across several domains, including automotive, manufacturing, retail, healthcare and many more, transforming businesses as an external machine learning department. We achieve this using our core expertise in state\-of\-the\-art machine learning combined with our culture of rapid iterations to build scalable solutions.




 This is a talent pool position open to multiple seniority levels. We are building a strong pipeline of Machine Learning Engineers to connect with when opportunities arise at Merantix Momentum. By joining our talent pool, you'll be among the first to be considered when we have openings that match your profile




**Your role**
* Scoping machine learning projects and assessing their technical feasibility through client interaction;
* Implementing machine learning methods and applying them to real\-world use cases;
* Contributing to the development and evolution of our internal AI stack and open source ecosystem;
* Collaborating with data, backend, and frontend engineers to build production\-ready AI solutions;
* Driving machine learning projects from ideation through to the production phase.


**Your profile**
 The ideal candidate is proficient in software engineering and the latest machine learning and deep learning technologies. You will independently scope, plan, manage, and drive machine learning projects from ideation to production.




 You are a great fit for our team if this describes you:




* MSc or PhD in computer science, Machine Learning, or related technical field;
* Strong programming skills in Python with experience in Deep Learning tasks and libraries like PyTorch;
* Experience with one or more cloud providers (Google Cloud Platform, AWS, Azure);
* Proven ability to independently complete complex, real\-world technical projects;
* Experience in time series analysis and at least one of the following: Computer Vision and/or Natural Language Processing and/or Graph Neural Networks and/or Reinforcement Learning and/or Causal Inference;
* Appreciation for sound engineering practices, including version control, clean code, code review, testing, CI/CD, and automation;
* Strong ability to interact with clients, understand their problems, and design and explain complex technical solutions;
* Fluency in English (German is a plus).


**What We Offer**
 What we offer




* We have a flexible work\-from\-home policy(hybrid);
* Brand new office situated on the AI Campus in Berlin;
* We offer Visa Sponsorship;
* Hardware allowance. We give you support to have all the equipment you would need to thrive in your job;
* International Team: within our current Team, we have more than 10 nationalities and counting;
* We offer 50€ per employee per month that can be allocated as desired to one of the following: Mobility \& transportation (NAVIT), sport (Urban Sports Club membership) or Edenred (Groceries);
* Engaging Topics and Excellence: Merantix offers unique insights into applied machine learning research and development, working with a group of highly talented engineers and entrepreneurs.
* Ethics: We are committed to developing ethical AI software;
* Dynamic working culture: We hold weekly and monthly events around AI Innovation and Implementation. We have a flat hierarchy, open 360° feedback, and flexible working hours;
* Learning and Development. Annual learning and development budget to attend conferences or purchase educational resources to further develop additional skills;


**About Us**
 We are an equal\-opportunity employer and value diversity. We consider all applications equally regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, or gender identity. We strongly encourage individuals from groups traditionally underrepresented in tech to apply, and we can help with immigration.

**Department:** IT Department, London


**Location:** Head Office (Cricklewood)


**Closing Date:** January 2, 2026


Job Summary


The Head of Data Innovation leads the strategic use of data to drive innovation, improve decision\-making, and enhance operational efficiency. This role bridges data science, analytics, and business strategy, fostering a culture of data\-driven innovation across the organization. Reporting to the Group IT Director.


**Main Responsibilities**


* Develop and implement a company\-wide data strategy aligned with business goals.
* Identify opportunities for innovation through data insights and emerging technologies.
* Lead cross\-functional teams in delivering data\-driven projects and proof\-of\-concepts.
* Build and maintain scalable data infrastructure (e.g., data lakes, pipelines).
* Ensure data quality, governance, and compliance with regulations.
* Translate complex data into actionable insights for non\-technical stakeholders.
* Mentor data scientists, analysts, and innovation specialists.
* Collaborate with leadership to embed data into strategic planning.
* Stay ahead of trends in AI, machine learning, and data tooling.




Essential Criteria


* Proven experience in data science, analytics, or innovation management.
* Strong leadership and communication skills.
* Familiarity with data platforms, visualization tools, and AI/ML technologies.
* Understanding of data governance and privacy regulations.
* Strategic thinker with a hands\-on approach to problem\-solving.


**Competencies \& Skills**


* Excellent written and spoken English with the ability to communicate clearly and at all levels;
* Excellent attention for detail;
* Ability to operate as a team player;
* Ability to work well under pressure;
* Excellent interpersonal and organisational skills;
* Must be proactive, methodical and results orientated;
* Ability to take accurate minutes of meetings;
* Highly organised, motivated and able to prioritise workload;
* Ability to manage own workload effectively and work to strict deadlines;
* Exceptional customer service skills with a natural flair of providing support and guidance and going ‘the extra mile’;
* Process driven and able to deliver results in a high volume;
* Ability to use initiative and identify solutions when a problem or difficult situation arises;
* Must be able to demonstrate credibility to build professional relationships with both employees and managers;
* Discreet when managing confidential matters;
* Ability to collate and interpret statistical data;
	+ Able to build lasting relationships with internal and external stakeholders/suppliers;
* An understanding/appreciation of the service requirements and the management of day to day operational issues;
* Ability to influence and persuade key decision makers;
Hours of Work


38 hrs per week


**The Equality Act**

Metroline is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment with due regard to legal obligations for protected characteristics i.e. age, disability, marriage and civil partnership, gender reassignment, pregnancy and maternity, race, religion and belief, sex and sexual orientation.


**How to apply**



Please email your CV and a cover letter to: vacancies@metroline.co.uk



Please ensure that the subject line of your email clearly indicates the position and vacancy code


**Applications**



Applications should include:


* the reasons you are applying for the post
* why you believe you are a suitable candidate
* any relevant qualifications or experience
